'''Richard Moon''' (born 1946) is an American [[aikido]] teacher,
executive coach, and peace activist holding the rank of 6th
''[[dan rank|dan]]''.<ref name="copyright-1946">{{cite
web |title=Copyright registrations — Richard Moon, 1946-
 |work=Copyright Encyclopedia |access-date=2026-09-21
 |url=https://www.copyrightencyclopedia.com/radical-militant-vegetarians-in-naziland-against-the-odds/}}</ref><ref name="nadeau-bio">{{cite web
 |title=Authors — Robert Nadeau Shihan
 |url=https://www.nadeaushihan.com/authors
 |access-date=2026-09-17}}</ref> He is the founder and chief instructor of
'''Aikido of Marin''' and a co-founder and senior instructor of City Aikido
of [[San Francisco]] with [[Robert Nadeau (aikidoka)|Robert Nadeau]].<ref
name="riai-bio">{{cite web
 |title=Richard Moon
 |work=Riai Aikido
 |url=http://www.conradedwards.net/riaiaikido/index.php/Main/RichardMoon
 |access-date=2026-09-17}}</ref>

== Early life and training ==

Moon began studying martial arts in 1969, training in [[Shotokan]] karate,
[[Kenpo]] and [[kung fu]] under various teachers. In 1971 he began his
study of aikido under Robert Nadeau, himself a personal student of aikido
founder [[Morihei Ueshiba]]; the student–teacher relationship has
continued for over fifty years.<ref name="nadeau-bio"/> Moon was also a
personal student of capoeira master [[Mestre Acordeon]] (Bira Almeida),
practiced Cheng Hsin with [[Peter Ralston]], and trained in [[qigong]]
with [[B. K. Frantzis]].<ref name="nadeau-bio"/><ref name="riai-bio"/>

In the early 1970s Moon was associated with the circle around
[[Jim Baker (Father Yod)|Jim Baker]] and worked at Baker's
[[The Source (restaurant)|Source restaurant]] on the [[Sunset Strip]]
and at the earlier Aware Inn.{{better source needed|date=September 2026}}

== Teaching career ==

By November 1980 Moon was teaching adult aikido classes at the Dance
Palace in [[Point Reyes Station, California]].<ref name="prl-1980">{{cite
news |title=Aikido (class listing) |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]]
 |date=1980-11-20 |page=13
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1125183831/}}</ref> In September
1983 he gave an aikido demonstration at the Dance Palace with David
Gamble and Sandy Jacobs,<ref name="prl-1983">{{cite news |title=Dance
Palace classes showcased |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]]
 |date=1983-09-08 |page=9
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1101135895/}}</ref> and by 1984 he
was teaching weekly aikido classes in West Marin.<ref name="prl-1984">{{
cite news |title=Classes (listing) |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]]
 |date=1984-09-06 |page=14
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1100933658/}}</ref>

In February 1985 Moon registered the [[fictitious business name]]
"Aikido of Marin" in [[Marin County, California|Marin County]].<ref
name="prl-fbn">{{cite news |title=Fictitious Business Name Statement —
Aikido of Marin, Richard Moon |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]]
 |date=1985-02-28 |page=16
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1100894910/}}</ref> The filing was
renewed in [[Novato, California|Novato]] in 1996.<ref name="novato-fbn">{{
cite news |title=Fictitious Business Name Statement — Aikido of Marin,
Richard Moon |newspaper=Novato Advance |date=1996-05-01 |page=23
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1100943036/}}</ref>

Moon developed "Aiki-Dance" / "Aikido and Dance", workshops blending
aikido movement with dance, offered in West Marin through the
1990s.<ref name="prl-1997">{{cite news |title=Aiki-Dance Workshop led by
Richard Moon |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]] |date=1997-04-17 |page=13
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1100842220/}}</ref><ref
name="prl-1998">{{cite news |title=Introduction to Aikido and Dance with
Richard Moon |newspaper=[[Point Reyes Light]] |date=1998-04-23 |page=13
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/1100916601/}}</ref>

With Chris Thorsen, Moon co-led "Aikido and Dialogue" programs through
their consultancy Performance Edge, applying aikido principles to
organizational learning and leadership training for corporate and
conference audiences.<ref name="hs-1997">{{cite news |title=conference
program — Chris Thorsen and Richard Moon: Aikido and Dialogue
 |newspaper=[[The Herald-Sun (Durham, North Carolina)|The Herald-Sun]]
 |location=Durham, NC |date=1997-10-07 |page=18
 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/793520210/}}</ref><ref
name="hs-2001">{{cite news |title=presenters listing — Chris Thorsen &
Richard Moon: Aikido |newspaper=[[The Herald-Sun (Durham, North
Carolina)|The Herald-Sun]] |location=Durham, NC |date=2001-09-23
 |page=80 |url=https://www.newspapers.com/image/795545627/}}</ref> He
also developed "Extraordinary Listening", a communications-training
program offered to community and business groups.<ref
name="xl-site">{{cite web |title=ExtraordinaryListening.com
 |work=Extraordinary Listening |url=http://extraordinarylistening.com/
 |access-date=2026-09-22}}</ref><ref name="linkedin-2025"/>

=== New Zealand ===

Moon has taught in New Zealand as a guest instructor since the late
1980s, when he was first invited by members of what became the Riai
Aikido community.<ref name="linkedin-2025">{{cite web |last=Moon
 |first=Richard |title=Just about to start last day teaching in New
Zealand |work=LinkedIn |date=2025-09-13
 |url=https://www.linkedin.com/posts/richard-moon-00891714_just-about-to-start-last-day-teaching-in-activity-7372723745481936896-fgKy
 |access-date=2026-09-17}}</ref> In March 2019 he taught alongside
Nadeau at the "O Sensei Revisited Down Under" workshop hosted by Riai
Aikido in [[Auckland]].<ref name="osensei-2019">{{cite web |title=O
Sensei Revisited Down Under |work=Riai Aikido
 |url=https://aikido.org.nz/nadeauworkshop/ |access-date=2026-09-17}}</ref>
He returned in September 2025 for a three-weekend seminar tour covering
the South Island, [[Wellington]] and the [[North Island]].<ref
name="linkedin-2025"/>

